01:01:44.870 --> 01:01:48.690
<v Nianshuang Wang>Yeah, that's what I hope. Yeah.
<v Nianshuang Wang>是的，那就是我希望的。是的。

01:01:48.690 --> 01:01:52.030
<v David Kestenbaum>What do your parents say?
<v David Kestenbaum>你的父母怎么说？

01:01:52.030 --> 01:02:12.650
<v Nianshuang Wang>My parents, actually, they don't know what I was doing. They just know, oh, you developed a vaccine. That's great. [LAUGHS] That's their thinking. They don't know how much contribution I did. Yeah, actually, they-- yeah, my mom got stroke several years ago. She may never know what I'm doing now, so.
<v Nianshuang Wang>我的父母，实际上，他们不知道我在做什么。他们只知道，噢，你开发了一种疫苗。那太棒了。[笑]那是他们的想法。他们不知道我贡献了多少。是的，实际上，他们——是的，我妈妈几年前中风了。她可能永远不知道我现在在做什么，所以。

01:02:12.650 --> 01:02:19.580
<v David  Kestenbaum>I'm sorry about your mom.
<v David  Kestenbaum>为你妈妈感到抱歉。

01:02:19.580 --> 01:02:30.420
<v Nianshuang Wang>Yeah, I'm a little sad about that. But she had encouraged a lot in the past, yeah. I will always remember those things, yeah.
<v Nianshuang Wang>是的，我为此有点难过。但她在过去鼓励了很多，是的。我永远会记得那些事，是的。

01:02:30.420 --> 01:02:58.000
<v David Kestenbaum>It can be hard, I think, when you're in deep with something complicated to explain that thing to someone on the outside, particularly with science. There's this version that often makes it out into the world of a single person having a clear, dramatic breakthrough-- Jonas Salk with the polio vaccine. The Nobel Prize is always given to one or a few people. But a lot of science isn't like that. I think most of it isn't.
<v David Kestenbaum>当你深入复杂的事情时，向局外人解释那件事可能会很困难，特别是科学。有一个版本通常会进入世界，即单个人有一个清晰、戏剧性的突破——乔纳斯·索尔克（Jonas Salk）和脊髓灰质炎疫苗。诺贝尔奖总是颁给一个人或几个人。但很多科学并不是那样的。我想大多数都不是。

01:02:58.000 --> 01:03:21.140
<v David Kestenbaum>When I asked Jason McClellan, the other scientist in this story, about his contribution to this, he started listing names, all the people whose work went before or whose ideas they adapted. Kizzmekia, when she gives talks, her last slides are just lists of names. It's never just one person pushing the rock up a hill.
<v David Kestenbaum>当我问贾森·麦克莱伦，这个故事里的另一位科学家，关于他对这个的贡献时，他开始列出名字，所有在他之前工作或者他们的想法被采纳的人。基兹梅基亚，当她演讲时，她的最后几张幻灯片只是名字列表。这从来不仅仅是一个人把石头推上山。

01:03:21.140 --> 01:03:38.750
<v Ira  Glass>David Kestenbaum is senior editor of our show. The NIH Moderna vaccine protected 94% of the people who got it in clinical trial. It was just this week approved for emergency use. The government has arranged to purchase 200 million doses.
<v Ira  Glass>大卫·凯斯滕鲍姆是我们节目的高级编辑。NIH Moderna疫苗在临床试验中保护了94%的人。它就在本周被批准用于紧急使用。政府已经安排购买2亿剂。

01:03:38.750 --> 01:03:48.860
